    "introduction": "George Schroeder competed for St. John's University in New York City on a full athletic grant for track & field. George has been teaching American History in high school since 1996, as well as coaching varsity track & field. He has been a competitive runner and cyclist since the late 1980's. George's first role was as background in the Russell Crow film Noah, which earned him his SAG waivers and membership in 2013. His first principal role came in the summer of 2015 as a stunt double for Bobby Cannavale in the HBO show Vinyl.",
